  "term": "occipital cortex",
  "definition": "The occipital cortex is a part of the brain discussed as a possible neural substrate, meaning a brain area whose function and connectivity may be linked to schizotypal traits. In the source, variation in the NOTCH4 gene is described as affecting how this brain region functions.",
